For W=7:  
Throughput = \(\frac{7 \times 4096}{0.604} \approx \frac{28672}{0.604} \approx 47470 \text{ b/s} \approx 47.5 \text{ kb/s}\)  

For W=17 and W=117, the sender transmits continuously at 64 kb/s (since window > pipe capacity). So throughput = 64 kb/s.  

Thus results:  
W=1: 6.8 kb/s  
W=7: 47.5 kb/s  
W=17: 64 kb/s  
W=117: 64 kb/s  

